\newlabel{tab:concentration}{{4}{5}{ASR concentration by attack category. Targeted attacks show highly concentrated ASR (Gini $>$ 0.7, top-1 judge contributes $>$56\% of panel ASR), providing mechanistic evidence for $\eta _{\max }$ dominance. Mann-Whitney $U$ test: $p < 0.001$ between categories}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Aggregation gradient under clustered SE. ``Neg.'' = fraction of significant $K_{\text  {eff}}$ coefficients that are negative. Bayesian calibration weakens $\eta _{\max }$ (11$\to $5/12) and flips $K_{\text  {eff}}$ direction (3/4 negative), while veto/threshold amplify the weakest-link channel.}}{5}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:aggregation}{{5}{5}{Aggregation gradient under clustered SE. ``Neg.'' = fraction of significant $K_{\text {eff}}$ coefficients that are negative. Bayesian calibration weakens $\eta _{\max }$ (11$\to $5/12) and flips $K_{\text {eff}}$ direction (3/4 negative), while veto/threshold amplify the weakest-link channel}{table.5}{}}
